# E2E test-count badge

The root `README.md` shows an E2E test-count badge:

```
[![E2E tests](https://img.shields.io/badge/E2E_tests-35-blue)](apps/e2e)
```

Whenever you add, remove, or rename `test(...)` cases in `apps/e2e/**/*.e2e.spec.ts`,
recount and update that number in the **same change**.

## Recount

Count `test(...)` cases (include `test.skip`/`test.only`/`test.fixme`; exclude
`test.describe`, `test.beforeEach`, `test.afterEach`):

```bash
rg -c -e "\\b(test|it)(\\.(skip|only|fixme))?\\s*\\(\\s*['\"\`]" apps/e2e/*.e2e.spec.ts \
  | awk -F: '{s+=$2} END {print s}'
```

Put the result into the badge URL (`E2E_tests-<N>-blue`). If the count is unchanged,
no edit is needed.
